  "sourceNotes": [
    "An official NWS Special Weather Statement includes Boyle County for patchy frost and locally dense river-valley fog through 9 AM EDT. No official NWS alert is active for the configured Clemson point; the Fire Danger Statement discussed by NWS Greenville-Spartanburg is confined to northeast Georgia.",
    "College of DuPage radar imagery showed no organized precipitation over either target region. True-color satellite imagery showed mostly clear conditions over Kentucky and the western Carolinas, with only thin high clouds approaching parts of Kentucky and the main coastal system remaining offshore.",
    "The October 20, 2026 Kentucky Weather Center post “A Boring and Beautiful Pattern Before Changes” was consulted as independent supplemental analysis. It supports dry skies, occasional thin high clouds, highs from the middle 60s to lower 70s and cool Kentucky nights; it is not an official source.",
    "KCEU resumed timely official reporting and is used again for current Upstate conditions and verification. Tempest data was not used.",
    "Official point forecasts, observations, office discussions and GFS/ECMWF benchmarks agree on a dry 72-hour pattern. The several-degree Thursday Upstate high-temperature difference is represented by the calibrated range; no unresolved material source conflict remains.",
    "HRRR, RAP, NAM, NAM 3-km Nest, GFS, GEFS and ECMWF availability was verified from official run files; College of DuPage panels supplied common visual context.",
    "Official NWS statements and alerts are separate from this independent analysis. Independent hazard probabilities and fire-spread concerns do not constitute watches, warnings or advisories."
  ],
